{
    "background_story": "Reagan was a free-spirited dance instructor with a passion for traditional Scottish folk dances. She spent most of her summers teaching at the Highland Games, where she would don her tartan skirt and lead the crowd in lively reels and jigs. But it was the schottische that held a special place in her heart. This lively, romantic dance had been passed down through her family for generations, and Reagan loved nothing more than to teach it to her students. As the music began, Reagan's eyes would sparkle, and she would glide across the dance floor, her feet moving in perfect time. Her love of the schottische was contagious, and soon her students were hooked, too. Under Reagan's guidance, they would twirl and spin, lost in the joy of the music and the magic of the dance.",
